-- The hostile reading: evidence for the findings of NOTES.md §4. Each assertion here states
-- the SURPRISING answer the encoding gives, so it passes; a reader should find each one wrong
-- in spirit. A finding that only reading can show is in NOTES.md alone, marked "reading only".

§ `Findings`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN class   IS A `A vehicle class in Annex I`
      licence IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A motor vehicle`
`a vehicle of class` class `needing a licence` licence MEANS
    `A motor vehicle` WITH
        `class in Annex I`                                          IS class
        `beyond its service life under the law`                     IS FALSE
        `a foreign vehicle temporarily imported for re-export, in traffic in Vietnam for less than 1 year` IS FALSE
        `remaining service life under the law of less than 1 year`  IS FALSE
        `subject to temporary registration`                         IS FALSE
        `a driving licence is required to drive it`                 IS licence

GIVEN roles IS A LIST OF STRING
      died  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person harmed in the accident`
`a person who is` roles `dying` died MEANS
    `A person harmed in the accident` WITH
        `driving the vehicle`                                     IS elem "driving" roles
        `on the vehicle`                                          IS elem "on the vehicle" roles
        `a passenger on the vehicle`                              IS elem "passenger" roles
        `the owner of the vehicle`                                IS FALSE
        `acted intentionally to cause the damage`                 IS FALSE
        `died`                                                    IS died
        `injuries`                                                IS EMPTY
        `damaged property`                                        IS EMPTY
        `amount agreed with the insured for health and life`      IS NOTHING
        `amount fixed by a court decision for health and life`    IS NOTHING
        `unidentified, or without a lawful heir`                  IS FALSE
        `actual necessary costs of burial and of keeping the remains to trace identity` IS 0

GIVEN `in traffic`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `under control`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `no licence`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `wholly a third party's fault` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An accident`
`an accident, in traffic` `in traffic` `, under control` `under control` `, no licence` `no licence` `, wholly a third party's fault` `wholly a third party's fault` MEANS
    `An accident` WITH
        `date of the accident`                                                         IS YMD 2026 8 3
        `the vehicle was participating in road traffic`                                 IS `in traffic`
        `the vehicle was moving, stopped or parked`                                     IS TRUE
        `the vehicle was under the control of its owner or a driver`                    IS `under control`
        `the owner had handed possession and use of the vehicle to another`             IS FALSE
        `the owner or the driver acted intentionally to cause the damage`              IS FALSE
        `the driver who caused it deliberately fled`                                    IS FALSE
        `the driver who fled had performed the owner's civil liability`                 IS FALSE
        `the driver did not meet the age condition of the Road Traffic Law`             IS FALSE
        `the driver had no driving licence`                                             IS `no licence`
        `the driver used an invalid driving licence`                                    IS FALSE
        `the driver's licence was erased or altered`                                    IS FALSE
        `the driver's licence had expired at the time of the accident`                  IS FALSE
        `the driver used a licence not matching the vehicle`                            IS FALSE
        `the driver's right to use the licence was suspended for a term, or the licence was revoked` IS FALSE
        `the driver's blood or breath alcohol exceeded the normal level in the Ministry of Health guidance` IS FALSE
        `the driver had used drugs or banned stimulants`                                IS FALSE
        `caused by war, terrorism or an earthquake`                                     IS FALSE
        `an authority found it caused entirely by the fault of a third party`           IS `wholly a third party's fault`
        `several motor vehicles caused it`                                              IS FALSE
        `the owner's share of the fault`                                                IS 1
        `the persons harmed`                                                            IS EMPTY

`an ordinary accident` MEANS `an accident, in traffic` TRUE `, under control` TRUE `, no licence` FALSE `, wholly a third party's fault` FALSE

§§ `R1 — a person on the vehicle who is not a passenger is covered by neither point of Article 7(1)`

-- Article 3(5)(a) takes "người trên xe" (persons on the vehicle) out of the third parties;
-- Article 7(1)(b) covers only "hành khách" (passengers). A person riding on the vehicle who is
-- not a passenger in the sense of a carriage (a family member on the back of a motorbike, a
-- crew member) is in neither. "Hành khách" is not defined in the sources (fork F25).
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "on the vehicle") `dying` TRUE) `an ordinary accident` (`a vehicle of class` (`a two-wheeled motorcycle` 110) `needing a licence` TRUE) EQUALS `outside the scope: the person is neither a third party nor a passenger`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026` (`a person who is` (LIST "on the vehicle") `dying` TRUE) `an ordinary accident` (`a vehicle of class` (`a two-wheeled motorcycle` 110) `needing a licence` TRUE) EQUALS `outside the scope: the person is neither a third party nor a passenger`

§§ `R2 — a vehicle parked unattended causes damage the insurance does not reach`

-- Article 3(2): an operating vehicle is moving, stopped or parked "có sự điều khiển" (under
-- the control of its owner or a driver); Article 3(3): in traffic means driven in road traffic.
-- A parked car with nobody at the wheel that rolls into a pedestrian is neither.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` TRUE) (`an accident, in traffic` FALSE `, under control` FALSE `, no licence` FALSE `, wholly a third party's fault` FALSE) (`a vehicle of class` (`a car not used for transport business` 5) `needing a licence` TRUE) EQUALS `outside the scope: the vehicle was neither in road traffic nor operating`

§§ `R3 — on its last-antecedent reading, Article 7(2)(c) excludes every unlicensed rider of a vehicle that needs no licence`

-- The encoding takes reading (ii) of fork F5. On the literal reading the qualifier "đối với xe
-- cơ giới bắt buộc phải có Giấy phép lái xe" governs only the last limb, so the cover for a
-- vehicle that needs no licence is illusory for any driver who has none.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 7(2)(c) — the driver's age or licence excludes the cover` (`an accident, in traffic` TRUE `, under control` TRUE `, no licence` TRUE `, wholly a third party's fault` FALSE) (`a vehicle of class` `an electric moped` `needing a licence` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Article 7(2)(c), on the last-antecedent reading — the driver's age or licence excludes the cover` (`an accident, in traffic` TRUE `, under control` TRUE `, no licence` TRUE `, wholly a third party's fault` FALSE) (`a vehicle of class` `an electric moped` `needing a licence` FALSE)

§§ `R4 — "entirely a third party's fault" halves an innocent third party's compensation`

-- Article 12(6)(a), third paragraph, keys the 50% on "lỗi hoàn toàn của người thứ ba", not on the
-- injured person's own fault. A pedestrian killed in an accident wholly caused by another third
-- party (say a cyclist who swerved) gets 75,000,000 instead of 150,000,000; the car's passenger in
-- the same accident gets the full 150,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` EMPTY `dying` TRUE) (`an accident, in traffic` TRUE `, under control` TRUE `, no licence` FALSE `, wholly a third party's fault` TRUE) EQUALS RIGHT 75000000
#ASSERT `Article 12(6)(a) — the compensation for the health and life of` `Decree 67/2023 as made` (`a person who is` (LIST "on the vehicle", "passenger") `dying` TRUE) (`an accident, in traffic` TRUE `, under control` TRUE `, no licence` FALSE `, wholly a third party's fault` TRUE) EQUALS RIGHT 150000000

§§ `R5 — Annex I charges a 16-seat business vehicle more than a 17-seat one`

-- Section V row 12, 16 seats: 3.054.000; row 13, 17 seats: 2.718.000. Every other step of
-- section V rises. The figure is the gazette's own (checked on the PDF page, NOTES.md §5.4).
-- src:2081 | 12 16 chỗ theo đăng ký 3.054.000
-- src:2082 | 13 17 chỗ theo đăng ký 2.718.000
#ASSERT `Annex I A.V — a car used for transport business, of` 16 GREATER THAN `Annex I A.V — a car used for transport business, of` 17
#ASSERT `Annex I A.V — a car used for transport business, of` 15 LESS THAN `Annex I A.V — a car used for transport business, of` 16

§§ `R6 — a band of Annex VI is a range of money, and nothing says who picks the point`

-- B.I 1.1 pays from 9,000,000 to 15,000,000. Neither Article 12 nor Annex VI says who fixes the
-- rate within 6-10% or by what criterion (only two notes, and only for three items, do).
#ASSERT `the payment band in Annex VI for` "B.I" "1.1" EQUALS RIGHT (`A payment band` OF 9000000, 15000000)

§§ `R9 — Article 9(3) sends a seller to Article 11, which has nothing for a seller`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11 states no refund for a termination on a change of owner, and this model does not invent one`

§§ `R12 — the insurer's discretion has a ceiling and no criterion`

-- Article 8(2): anything from 85% to 115% of the Annex I premium; Article 12(7): any reduction up
-- to 5%. Both ends are lawful on the same facts.
#ASSERT `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` (0 MINUS 15%) `to` 437000 EQUALS RIGHT 371450
#ASSERT `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` (15%) `to` 437000 EQUALS RIGHT 502550

§§ `R14 — special case 1 can halve what the table's own stiffness rows pay`

-- The middle finger: the table's row for stiffness of its interphalangeal joints ("Cứng các khớp
-- liên đốt", B.VI 4.5.3.3) pays 7-9%; special case 1, for stiffness ("dính các khớp") of a finger
-- other than the thumb and index, pays 50% of its loss (B.VI 4.5.3.6, 8-10%): 4-5%.
#ASSERT `the payment band in Annex VI for` "B.VI" "4.5.3.3" EQUALS RIGHT (`A payment band` OF 10500000, 13500000)
#ASSERT `Annex VI — the rate in percent for the injury` (`stiffness of the joints of a digit, special case 1` FALSE "B.VI" "4.5.3.6" (JUST 10)) EQUALS RIGHT 5

§§ `R15 — the premium arithmetic of section B`

-- A 1-day contract costs the same as a 30-day one: a twelfth of the year. A two-year term that
-- spans 29 February costs more than two years' premium (731/365), one that does not costs exactly
-- two (730/365).
#ASSERT `Annex I section B — the premium for a term of` 1 `days, on an annual premium of` 437000 EQUALS `Annex I section B — the premium for a term of` 30 `days, on an annual premium of` 437000
#ASSERT `Annex I section B — the premium for a term of` 731 `days, on an annual premium of` 437000 GREATER THAN 874000
